IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr2-helpers`

-- CHAPTER 2 OF PART 3 -- ENHANCED CUSTOMER DUE DILIGENCE (regulations 33 to 36) of the Money Laundering,
-- Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692),
-- United Kingdom.  Lines 1009-1169 of the text.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- LAYER 1: THE LAW, OBJECTIVELY.  Each rule follows the text's own structure and carries its citation.
-- A rule answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (a MAYBE BOOLEAN): JUST FALSE only where the text says
-- no in its own words, NOTHING where it does not answer.  Every branch says which, and why.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ANOTHER SECTION ANSWERS (seams, see NOTES.md "Seams (mlr2)"):
--   S-8   `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`     (every rule that begins "A relevant person ...")
--   S-K1  `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`
--   S-1   `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures`
-- Facts that a witness of ordinary competence could state are BOOLEANs, dates and numbers.

§ `Chapter 2 -- Enhanced customer due diligence (regulations 33 to 36)`

§§ `Regulation 33 -- Obligation to apply enhanced customer due diligence`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 33(3)(a), (b), (c): the three definitions that paragraph (1)(b) uses.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1030 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b)—
@ref reg 33(3) (src:1030-1030)
-- src:1031 | (a) a “FATF call for action country” means a country named on the list of High-Risk Jurisdictions subject to a Call for Action published by the Financial Action Task Force as such list has effect from time to time;
@ref reg 33(3)(a) (src:1031-1031)
GIVEN `the country is named on the list of High-Risk Jurisdictions subject to a Call for Action published by the Financial Action Task Force, as that list has effect on the date asked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(3)(a) the country is a FATF call for action country` MEANS
    IF `the country is named on the list of High-Risk Jurisdictions subject to a Call for Action published by the Financial Action Task Force, as that list has effect on the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a country named on the list"

-- reg 33(3)(b): S-1 answers whether the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27.
-- SEAM S-1 (asking)
-- src:1032 | (b) a “relevant transaction” means a transaction in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27;
@ref reg 33(3)(b) (src:1032-1032)
GIVEN `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(3)(b) the transaction is a relevant transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a transaction in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 27 has not answered

-- src:1033 | (c) being “established in” a country means—
-- src:1034 | (i) in the case of a legal person, being incorporated in or having its principal place of business in that country, or, in the case of a financial institution or a credit institution, having its principal regulatory authority in that country; and
-- src:1035 | (ii) in the case of an individual, being resident in that country, but not merely having been born in that country.
@ref reg 33(3)(c) (src:1033-1035)
DECLARE `reg 33(3)(c) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 33(3)(c)(i) a legal person other than a financial institution or a credit institution`
    `reg 33(3)(c)(i) a financial institution or a credit institution`
    `reg 33(3)(c)(ii) an individual`

DECLARE `reg 33(3)(c) the person and the country` HAS
    `kind of person` IS A `reg 33(3)(c) kind of person`
    `incorporated in the country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has its principal place of business in the country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has its principal regulatory authority in the country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in the country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `born in the country` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 33(3)(c) (src:1033-1035)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 33(3)(c) the person and the country`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(3)(c) the person is established in the country` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `kind of person`
    WHEN `reg 33(3)(c)(i) a legal person other than a financial institution or a credit institution` THEN
        IF facts's `incorporated in the country` OR facts's `has its principal place of business in the country`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "being 'established in' a country means ... in the case of a legal person, being incorporated in or having its principal place of business in that country"
    WHEN `reg 33(3)(c)(i) a financial institution or a credit institution` THEN
        IF facts's `incorporated in the country` OR facts's `has its principal place of business in the country` OR facts's `has its principal regulatory authority in the country`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or, in the case of a financial institution or a credit institution, having its principal regulatory authority in that country"
    WHEN `reg 33(3)(c)(ii) an individual` THEN
        -- facts's `born in the country` is not read: "but not merely having been born in that country"
        IF facts's `resident in the country`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an individual, being resident in that country, but not merely having been born in that country"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 33(1)(b): the FATF limb, built from the three definitions above.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- SEAM S-K1 (asking), SEAM S-1 (asking, through reg 33(3)(b))
-- src:1015 | (b) in any business relationship ... with a person established in a FATF call for action country or in relation to any relevant transaction where either of the parties to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country;
@ref reg 33(1)(b) (src:1015-1015)
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person the business relationship is with is established in a FATF call for action country` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 33(3)(b) the transaction is a relevant transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `either of the parties to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(1)(b) the business relationship or transaction is connected with a FATF call for action country` MEANS
    -- the text names two routes ("in any business relationship ... with a person established in a FATF call for action country or in relation to any relevant transaction where either of the parties to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country"); each route is "yes" when both its parts are, "no" when one part is answered no, and the limb is "no" when both routes are "no" (a limb introduced by "in any ... where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any business relationship ... with a person established in a FATF call for action country or in relation to any relevant transaction where either of the parties ... is established" (a relationship with a person not so established, and no relevant transaction with such a party, is neither route)
    `mlr2 either is true`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` `the person the business relationship is with is established in a FATF call for action country`)
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 33(3)(b) the transaction is a relevant transaction` `either of the parties to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 33(1): the duty itself (seam S-3 answered here).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1011 | (1) A relevant person must apply enhanced customer due diligence measures and enhanced ongoing monitoring, in addition to the customer due diligence measures required under regulation 28 and, if applicable, regulation 29, to manage and mitigate the risks arising—
-- src:1012 | (a) in any case identified as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing—
-- src:1013 | (i) by the relevant person under regulation 18(1), or
-- src:1014 | (ii) in information made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47;
-- src:1015 | (b) in any business relationship ... with a person established in a FATF call for action country or in relation to any relevant transaction where either of the parties to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country;
-- src:1016 | (c) in relation to correspondent relationships with a credit institution or a financial institution (in accordance with regulation 34);
-- src:1017 | (d) if a relevant person has determined that a customer or potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP (in accordance with regulation 35);
-- src:1018 | (e) in any case where the relevant person discovers that a customer has provided false or stolen identification documentation or information and the relevant person proposes to continue to deal with that customer;
-- src:1019 | (f) in any case where—
-- src:1020 | (i) a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large in each case given the nature of the transaction,
-- src:1021 | (ii) there is an unusual pattern of transactions, or
-- src:1022 | (iii) the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose, and
-- src:1023 | (g) in any other case which by its nature can present a higher risk of money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref reg 33(1) (src:1011-1023)
DECLARE `reg 33(1) the case` HAS
    `the relevant person's risk assessment under regulation 18(1) identified the case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `information made available under regulations 17(9) and 47 identified the case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reg 33(1)(b) the business relationship or transaction is connected with a FATF call for action country` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the case is a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person has determined that the customer or potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person has discovered that the customer has provided false or stolen identification documentation or information, and proposes to continue to deal with that customer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, in each case given the nature of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is an unusual pattern of transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the case by its nature can present a higher risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN

-- SEAM S-3 (answering), SEAM S-8 (asking)
@ref reg 33(1) (src:1011-1023)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `reg 33(1) the case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the answer for a relevant person`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            facts's `the relevant person's risk assessment under regulation 18(1) identified the case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing`
            OR facts's `information made available under regulations 17(9) and 47 identified the case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing`
        `limb (c)` MEANS facts's `the case is a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or a financial institution`
        `limb (d)` MEANS facts's `the relevant person has determined that the customer or potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP`
        `limb (e)` MEANS facts's `the relevant person has discovered that the customer has provided false or stolen identification documentation or information, and proposes to continue to deal with that customer`
        `limb (f)` MEANS
            facts's `a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, in each case given the nature of the transaction`
            OR facts's `there is an unusual pattern of transactions`
            OR facts's `the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose`
        `limb (g)` MEANS facts's `the case by its nature can present a higher risk of money laundering or terrorist financing`
        `the answer for a relevant person` MEANS
            -- A limb that holds gives JUST TRUE.  Every limb is introduced by "in any case identified", "in any case where" or "if", and limb (g) catches "any other case which by its nature can present a higher risk": when no limb holds the answer is no.
            -- NOTHING arises only from limb (b), whose seams (regulations 4 and 27) may be unanswered.
            `mlr2 either is true`
                (IF `limb (a)` OR `limb (c)` OR `limb (d)` OR `limb (e)` OR `limb (f)` OR `limb (g)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any case identified as one where there is a high risk ...", "in any case where ...", "if a relevant person has determined ...", and (g) "in any other case which by its nature can present a higher risk": a case in none of them is not a case for enhanced due diligence (a failed "where"/"if", ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
                (facts's `reg 33(1)(b) the business relationship or transaction is connected with a FATF call for action country`)

-- reg 33(1): the enhanced measures are "in addition to the customer due diligence measures required under regulation 28 and, if applicable, regulation 29".
-- A compliance check of a duty that has arisen (marginal reading (c)): an undischarged "must" is a "no".  Where the duty has not arisen, or is not known to have, the check does not arise.
@ref reg 33(1) (src:1011-1011)
GIVEN `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has applied enhanced customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has applied enhanced ongoing monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has also applied the customer due diligence measures required under regulation 28 and, if applicable, regulation 29` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(1) the relevant person has applied the enhanced measures in addition to the regulation 28 measures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the relevant person has applied enhanced customer due diligence measures`
           AND `the relevant person has applied enhanced ongoing monitoring`
           AND `the relevant person has also applied the customer due diligence measures required under regulation 28 and, if applicable, regulation 29`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must apply enhanced customer due diligence measures and enhanced ongoing monitoring, in addition to the customer due diligence measures required under regulation 28 and, if applicable, regulation 29" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): there is no duty to check: regulation 33(1) does not require enhanced measures, and this check asks only whether a duty that arose was discharged
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulation 33(1) requires enhanced measures has not been answered

-- src:1024 | (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply when the customer is a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity which is established in a third country if all the following conditions are satisfied—
-- src:1025 | (a) the entity is—
-- src:1026 | (i) subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive); and
-- src:1027 | (ii) supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive;
-- src:1028 | (b) the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under requirements equivalent to those laid down in Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive; and
-- src:1029 | (c) the relevant person, applying a risk-based approach, does not consider that it is necessary to apply enhanced customer due diligence measures.
@ref reg 33(2) (src:1024-1029)
GIVEN `the customer is a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity which is established in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under requirements equivalent to those laid down in Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person, applying a risk-based approach, does not consider that it is necessary to apply enhanced customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(2) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the customer is a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity which is established in a third country`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply when the customer is a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity which is established in a third country" ("when" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling)
        IF `the entity is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity`
           AND `the entity is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive`
           AND `the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under requirements equivalent to those laid down in Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive`
           AND `the relevant person, applying a risk-based approach, does not consider that it is necessary to apply enhanced customer due diligence measures`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all the following conditions are satisfied"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 33(3A) and (4): what the enhanced measures taken for paragraph (1)(b) and (1)(f) must include.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1036 | (3A) The enhanced due diligence measures taken by a relevant person for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b) must include—
-- src:1037 | (a) obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer’s beneficial owner;
-- src:1038 | (b) obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business relationship;
-- src:1039 | (c) obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth of the customer and of the customer’s beneficial owner;
-- src:1040 | (d) obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions;
-- src:1041 | (e) obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing or continuing the business relationship;
-- src:1042 | (f) conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship by increasing the number and timing of controls applied, and selecting patterns of transactions that need further examination.
@ref reg 33(3A) (src:1036-1042)
DECLARE `reg 33(3A) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 33(3A)(a) obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer's`
    `reg 33(3A)(b) obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business`
    `reg 33(3A)(c) obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth`
    `reg 33(3A)(d) obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions`
    `reg 33(3A)(e) obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing`
    `reg 33(3A)(f) conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship`
    `reg 33(3A) another measure`

@ref reg 33(3A) (src:1036-1042)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 33(3A) measure`
`reg 33(3A) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 33(3A)(a) obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer's`
    , `reg 33(3A)(b) obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business`
    , `reg 33(3A)(c) obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth`
    , `reg 33(3A)(d) obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions`
    , `reg 33(3A)(e) obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing`
    , `reg 33(3A)(f) conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship`

-- reg 33(3A): the six measures that the enhanced measures taken for paragraph (1)(b) must include (a minimum, not a closed list).
@ref reg 33(3A) (src:1036-1042)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(3A) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(3A) the measure must be included` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(a) obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer's` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(b) obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(c) obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(d) obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(e) obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(f) conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must include" fixes a minimum and the paragraph does not say that nothing else may be included

@ref reg 33(3A) (src:1036-1042)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(3A) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 33(3A) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(a) obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer's` THEN JUST "obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer’s beneficial owner"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(b) obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business` THEN JUST "obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business relationship"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(c) obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth` THEN JUST "obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth of the customer and of the customer’s beneficial owner"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(d) obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions` THEN JUST "obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(e) obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing` THEN JUST "obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing or continuing the business relationship"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A)(f) conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship` THEN JUST "conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship by increasing the number and timing of controls applied, and selecting patterns of transactions that need further examination"
    WHEN `reg 33(3A) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

@ref reg 33(3A) (src:1036-1042)
GIVEN `the enhanced measures are taken for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures taken` IS A LIST OF `reg 33(3A) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(3A) the enhanced measures taken include every measure that the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the enhanced measures are taken for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b)"
        IF all (GIVEN measure YIELD elem measure `the measures taken`) `reg 33(3A) the entries listed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include" (a measure the paragraph requires is missing; marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- src:1043 | (4) The enhanced customer due diligence measures taken by a relevant person for the purpose of paragraph (1)(f) must include—
-- src:1044 | (a) as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose of the transaction, and
-- src:1045 | (b) increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business relationship in which the transaction is made to determine whether that transaction or that relationship appear to be suspicious.
@ref reg 33(4) (src:1043-1045)
DECLARE `reg 33(4) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 33(4)(a) as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose`
    `reg 33(4)(b) increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business`
    `reg 33(4) another measure`

@ref reg 33(4) (src:1043-1045)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 33(4) measure`
`reg 33(4) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 33(4)(a) as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose`
    , `reg 33(4)(b) increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business`

-- reg 33(4): the two measures that the enhanced measures taken for paragraph (1)(f) must include.
@ref reg 33(4) (src:1043-1045)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(4) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(4) the measure must be included` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(4)(a) as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(4)(b) increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must include"
    WHEN `reg 33(4) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must include" fixes a minimum and the paragraph does not say that nothing else may be included

@ref reg 33(4) (src:1043-1045)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(4) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 33(4) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(4)(a) as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose` THEN JUST "as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose of the transaction"
    WHEN `reg 33(4)(b) increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business` THEN JUST "increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business relationship in which the transaction is made to determine whether that transaction or that relationship appear to be suspicious"
    WHEN `reg 33(4) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

@ref reg 33(4) (src:1043-1045)
GIVEN `the enhanced measures are taken for the purpose of paragraph (1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures taken` IS A LIST OF `reg 33(4) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(4) the enhanced measures taken include every measure that the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the enhanced measures are taken for the purpose of paragraph (1)(f)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of paragraph (1)(f)"
        IF all (GIVEN measure YIELD elem measure `the measures taken`) `reg 33(4) the entries listed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include" (a measure the paragraph requires is missing; marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

