-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1046 | (4A) Where a relevant person provides a life insurance policy, the relevant person must consider the nature and identity of the beneficiary of the policy when assessing whether there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing, and the extent of the measures which should be taken to manage and mitigate that risk.
@ref reg 33(4A) (src:1046-1046)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person provides a life insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(4A) the relevant person must consider the nature and identity of the beneficiary of the policy` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person provides a life insurance policy`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a relevant person provides a life insurance policy" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1047 | (4B) Where the beneficiary of a life insurance policy provided by a relevant person—
-- src:1048 | (a) is a legal person or a legal arrangement, and
-- src:1049 | (b) presents a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing,
-- src:1050 | the relevant person must take reasonable measures to identify and verify the identity of the beneficial owner of that beneficiary before any payment is made under the policy.
@ref reg 33(4B) (src:1047-1050)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary of the life insurance policy provided by the relevant person is a legal person or a legal arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary presents a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(4B) the relevant person must take reasonable measures to identify and verify the identity of the beneficial owner of the beneficiary` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the beneficiary of the life insurance policy provided by the relevant person is a legal person or a legal arrangement` AND `the beneficiary presents a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the beneficiary of a life insurance policy provided by a relevant person (a) is a legal person or a legal arrangement, and (b) presents a high risk" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- The time limit: "before any payment is made under the policy".  A date the measures were taken (NOTHING if they
-- have not been) and the date of the payment (NOTHING if none has been made).
@ref reg 33(4B) (src:1047-1050)
GIVEN `the date on which the measures were taken` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which a payment was made under the policy` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(4B) the measures were taken before any payment was made under the policy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which a payment was made under the policy`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no payment has been made, so the time limit "before any payment is made" has not yet been missed or met
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST payment THEN
        CONSIDER `the date on which the measures were taken`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before any payment is made under the policy" (a payment has been made and the measures have not been taken)
        WHEN JUST measures THEN
            IF measures LESS THAN payment
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before any payment is made under the policy" (taken on or after the day of the payment)

-- src:1051 | (5) Depending on the requirements of the case, the enhanced customer due diligence measures required under paragraph (1) may also include, among other things—
-- src:1052 | (a) seeking additional independent, reliable sources to verify information provided or made available to the relevant person;
-- src:1053 | (b) taking additional measures to understand better the background, ownership and financial situation of the customer, and other parties to the transaction;
-- src:1054 | (c) taking further steps to be satisfied that the transaction is consistent with the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship;
-- src:1055 | (d) increasing the monitoring of the business relationship, including greater scrutiny of transactions.
@ref reg 33(5) (src:1051-1055)
DECLARE `reg 33(5) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 33(5)(a) seeking additional independent, reliable sources to verify information`
    `reg 33(5)(b) taking additional measures to understand better the background`
    `reg 33(5)(c) taking further steps to be satisfied that the transaction is consistent`
    `reg 33(5)(d) increasing the monitoring of the business relationship, including`
    `reg 33(5) another measure`

@ref reg 33(5) (src:1051-1055)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 33(5) measure`
`reg 33(5) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 33(5)(a) seeking additional independent, reliable sources to verify information`
    , `reg 33(5)(b) taking additional measures to understand better the background`
    , `reg 33(5)(c) taking further steps to be satisfied that the transaction is consistent`
    , `reg 33(5)(d) increasing the monitoring of the business relationship, including`

-- reg 33(5): measures that the enhanced measures may also include, depending on the requirements of the case.
@ref reg 33(5) (src:1051-1055)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(5) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(5) the measure may be included` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(a) seeking additional independent, reliable sources to verify information` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "may also include, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(b) taking additional measures to understand better the background` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "may also include, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(c) taking further steps to be satisfied that the transaction is consistent` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "may also include, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(d) increasing the monitoring of the business relationship, including` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "may also include, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(5) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may also include, among other things" leaves other measures open

@ref reg 33(5) (src:1051-1055)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(5) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 33(5) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(a) seeking additional independent, reliable sources to verify information` THEN JUST "seeking additional independent, reliable sources to verify information provided or made available to the relevant person"
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(b) taking additional measures to understand better the background` THEN JUST "taking additional measures to understand better the background, ownership and financial situation of the customer, and other parties to the transaction"
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(c) taking further steps to be satisfied that the transaction is consistent` THEN JUST "taking further steps to be satisfied that the transaction is consistent with the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship"
    WHEN `reg 33(5)(d) increasing the monitoring of the business relationship, including` THEN JUST "increasing the monitoring of the business relationship, including greater scrutiny of transactions"
    WHEN `reg 33(5) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- src:1056 | (6) When assessing whether there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent of the measures which should be taken to manage and mitigate that risk, relevant persons must take account of risk factors including, among other things—
-- src:1057 | (a) customer risk factors, including whether—
-- src:1058 | (i) the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances;
-- src:1059 | (ii) the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk (see sub-paragraph (c));
-- src:1060 | (iii) the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle for holding personal assets;
-- src:1061 | (iv) the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares in bearer form;
-- src:1062 | (v) the customer is a business that is cash intensive;
-- src:1063 | (vi) the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively complex given the nature of the company's business;
-- src:1064 | (vii) the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy;
-- src:1065 | (viii) the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence rights in or citizenship of a state in exchange for transfers of capital, purchase of a property, government bonds or investment in corporate entities in that state;
-- src:1066 | (b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors, including whether—
-- src:1067 | (i) the product involves private banking;
-- src:1068 | (ii) the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity;
-- src:1069 | (iii) the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships or transactions, without certain safeguards, such as an electronic identification process which meets the conditions set out in regulation 28(19);
-- src:1070 | (iv) payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties;
-- src:1071 | (v) new products and new business practices are involved, including new delivery mechanisms, and the use of new or developing technologies for both new and pre-existing products;
-- src:1072 | (vi) the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee shareholders or shadow directors, or the formation of companies in a third country;
-- src:1073 | (vii) there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco products, cultural artefacts, ivory or other items related to protected species, or other items of archaeological, historical, cultural or religious significance or of rare scientific value;
-- src:1074 | (c) geographical risk factors, including—
-- src:1075 | (i) countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports, as not having effective systems to counter money laundering or terrorist financing;
-- src:1076 | (ii) countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels of corruption or other criminal activity, such as terrorism (within the meaning of section 1 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ), money laundering, and the production and supply of illicit drugs;
-- src:1077 | (iii) countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued by, for example, the European Union or the United Nations;
-- src:1078 | (iv) countries providing funding or support for terrorism;
-- src:1079 | (v) countries that have organisations operating within their territory which have been designated—
-- src:1080 | (aa) by the government of the United Kingdom as proscribed organisations under Schedule 2 to the Terrorism Act 2000 , or
-- src:1081 | (bb) by other countries, international organisations or the European Union as terrorist organisations;
-- src:1082 | (vi) countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports published by the Financial Action Task Force, the International Monetary Fund, the World Bank, the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development or other international bodies or non-governmental organisations as not implementing requirements to counter money laundering and terrorist financing that are consistent with the recommendations published by the Financial Action Task Force in February 2012 and updated in June 2019.
@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
DECLARE `reg 33(6) risk factor` IS ONE OF
    `reg 33(6)(a)(i) the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(ii) the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(iii) the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(iv) the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(v) the customer is a business that is cash intensive`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(vi) the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(vii) the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy`
    `reg 33(6)(a)(viii) the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(i) the product involves private banking`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(ii) the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(iii) the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(iv) payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(v) new products and new business practices are involved, including new`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(vi) the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee`
    `reg 33(6)(b)(vii) there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco`
    `reg 33(6)(c)(i) countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations`
    `reg 33(6)(c)(ii) countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels`
    `reg 33(6)(c)(iii) countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued`
    `reg 33(6)(c)(iv) countries providing funding or support for terrorism`
    `reg 33(6)(c)(v) countries that have organisations operating within their territory`
    `reg 33(6)(c)(vi) countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed`
    `reg 33(6) another risk factor`

@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 33(6) risk factor`
`reg 33(6) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 33(6)(a)(i) the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(ii) the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(iii) the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(iv) the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(v) the customer is a business that is cash intensive`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(vi) the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(vii) the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy`
    , `reg 33(6)(a)(viii) the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(i) the product involves private banking`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(ii) the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(iii) the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(iv) payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(v) new products and new business practices are involved, including new`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(vi) the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee`
    , `reg 33(6)(b)(vii) there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco`
    , `reg 33(6)(c)(i) countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations`
    , `reg 33(6)(c)(ii) countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels`
    , `reg 33(6)(c)(iii) countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued`
    , `reg 33(6)(c)(iv) countries providing funding or support for terrorism`
    , `reg 33(6)(c)(v) countries that have organisations operating within their territory`
    , `reg 33(6)(c)(vi) countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed`

-- reg 33(6): the risk factors a relevant person must take account of when assessing whether there is a high risk (customer, product and geographical factors).
@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(6) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(6) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(i) the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(ii) the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(iii) the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(iv) the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(v) the customer is a business that is cash intensive` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(vi) the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(vii) the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(viii) the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(i) the product involves private banking` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(ii) the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(iii) the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(iv) payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(v) new products and new business practices are involved, including new` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(vi) the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(vii) there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(i) countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(ii) countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(iii) countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(iv) countries providing funding or support for terrorism` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(v) countries that have organisations operating within their territory` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(vi) countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 33(6) another risk factor` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including, among other things" leaves other risk factors open

@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(6) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 33(6) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(i) the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances` THEN JUST "the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(ii) the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk` THEN JUST "the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk (see sub-paragraph (c))"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(iii) the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle` THEN JUST "the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle for holding personal assets"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(iv) the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares` THEN JUST "the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares in bearer form"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(v) the customer is a business that is cash intensive` THEN JUST "the customer is a business that is cash intensive"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(vi) the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively` THEN JUST "the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively complex given the nature of the company's business"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(vii) the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy` THEN JUST "the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(viii) the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence` THEN JUST "the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence rights in or citizenship of a state in exchange for transfers of capital, purchase of a property, government bonds or investment in corporate entities in that state"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(i) the product involves private banking` THEN JUST "the product involves private banking"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(ii) the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity` THEN JUST "the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(iii) the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships` THEN JUST "the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships or transactions, without certain safeguards, such as an electronic identification process which meets the conditions set out in regulation 28(19)"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(iv) payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties` THEN JUST "payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(v) new products and new business practices are involved, including new` THEN JUST "new products and new business practices are involved, including new delivery mechanisms, and the use of new or developing technologies for both new and pre-existing products"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(vi) the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee` THEN JUST "the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee shareholders or shadow directors, or the formation of companies in a third country"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(vii) there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco` THEN JUST "there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco products, cultural artefacts, ivory or other items related to protected species, or other items of archaeological, historical, cultural or religious significance or of rare scientific value"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(i) countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations` THEN JUST "countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports, as not having effective systems to counter money laundering or terrorist financing"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(ii) countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels` THEN JUST "countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels of corruption or other criminal activity, such as terrorism (within the meaning of section 1 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ), money laundering, and the production and supply of illicit drugs"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(iii) countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued` THEN JUST "countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued by, for example, the European Union or the United Nations"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(iv) countries providing funding or support for terrorism` THEN JUST "countries providing funding or support for terrorism"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(v) countries that have organisations operating within their territory` THEN JUST "countries that have organisations operating within their territory which have been designated— (aa) by the government of the United Kingdom as proscribed organisations under Schedule 2 to the Terrorism Act 2000 , or (bb) by other countries, international organisations or the European Union as terrorist organisations"
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(vi) countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed` THEN JUST "countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports published by the Financial Action Task Force, the International Monetary Fund, the World Bank, the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development or other international bodies or non-governmental organisations as not implementing requirements to counter money laundering and terrorist financing that are consistent with the recommendations published by the Financial Action Task Force in February 2012 and updated in June 2019"
    WHEN `reg 33(6) another risk factor` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 33(6): the three headings under which the risk factors are listed.  The text names them "(a) customer risk factors", "(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors" and "(c) geographical risk factors".
DECLARE `reg 33(6) heading` IS ONE OF
    `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors`
    `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors`
    `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors`

@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 33(6) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 33(6) heading`
`reg 33(6) the heading under which the risk factor is listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(i) the business relationship is conducted in unusual circumstances` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(ii) the customer is resident in a geographical area of high risk` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(iii) the customer is a legal person or legal arrangement that is a vehicle` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(iv) the customer is a company that has nominee shareholders or shares` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(v) the customer is a business that is cash intensive` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(vi) the corporate structure of the customer is unusual or excessively` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(vii) the customer is the beneficiary of a life insurance policy` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(a)(viii) the customer is a third country national who is applying for residence` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(a) customer risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(i) the product involves private banking` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(ii) the product or transaction is one which might favour anonymity` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(iii) the situation involves non-face-to-face business relationships` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(iv) payments will be received from unknown or unassociated third parties` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(v) new products and new business practices are involved, including new` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(vi) the service involves the provision of nominee directors, nominee` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(b)(vii) there is a transaction related to oil, arms, precious metals, tobacco` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(i) countries identified by credible sources, such as mutual evaluations` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(ii) countries identified by credible sources as having significant levels` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(iii) countries subject to sanctions, embargos or similar measures issued` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(iv) countries providing funding or support for terrorism` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(v) countries that have organisations operating within their territory` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6)(c)(vi) countries identified by credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed` THEN JUST `reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors` -- listed: under reg 33(6)(c) geographical risk factors
    WHEN `reg 33(6) another risk factor` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): a factor outside the list is under no heading the text gives

-- How many of the listed risk factors stand under a heading (a count of the entries of the list, not a rule of the text).
@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
GIVEN heading IS A `reg 33(6) heading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 33(6) the number of listed risk factors under the heading` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN factor YIELD `reg 33(6) the heading under which the risk factor is listed` factor EQUALS JUST heading) `reg 33(6) the entries listed`)

-- reg 33(6): "When assessing whether there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent of the measures which should be taken to manage and mitigate that risk, relevant persons must take account of risk factors".
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
@ref reg 33(6) (src:1056-1082)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is assessing whether there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent of the measures which should be taken to manage and mitigate that risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `reg 33(6) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(6) the relevant person must take account of the risk factor when assessing` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person is assessing whether there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent of the measures which should be taken to manage and mitigate that risk`
         THEN `reg 33(6) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` item
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When assessing whether there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in a particular situation" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))


-- reg 33(7): "may not always indicate" -- the presence of risk factors does not decide the question either way.
-- src:1083 | (7) In making the assessment referred to in paragraph (6), relevant persons must bear in mind that the presence of one or more risk factors may not always indicate that there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in a particular situation.
@ref reg 33(7) (src:1083-1083)
GIVEN `the number of risk factors present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 33(7) the presence of the risk factors indicates a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` MEANS
    IF `the number of risk factors present` AT LEAST 1
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the presence of one or more risk factors may not always indicate that there is a high risk"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks of "one or more risk factors"; it says nothing where none is present

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 34 -- credit institutions, financial institutions and correspondent relationships.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Regulation 34 -- Enhanced customer due diligence: credit institutions, financial institutions and correspondent relationships`

-- src:1086 | (1) A credit institution or financial institution (the “correspondent”) which has or proposes to have a correspondent relationship involving the execution of payments with another such institution (the “respondent”) from a third country must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33—
-- src:1087 | (a) gather sufficient information about the respondent to understand fully the nature of its business;
-- src:1088 | (b) determine from publicly-available information from credible sources the reputation of the respondent and the quality of the supervision to which the respondent is subject;
-- src:1089 | (c) assess the respondent's controls to counter money laundering and terrorist financing;
-- src:1090 | (d) obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new correspondent relationship;
-- src:1091 | (e) document the responsibilities of the respondent and correspondent in the correspondent relationship; and
-- src:1092 | (f) be satisfied that, in respect of those of the respondent's customers who have direct access to accounts with the correspondent, the respondent—
-- src:1093 | (i) has verified the identity of, and conducts ongoing customer due diligence measures in relation to, such customers; and
-- src:1094 | (ii) is able to provide to the correspondent, upon request, the documents or information obtained when applying such customer due diligence measures.
@ref reg 34(1) (src:1086-1094)
DECLARE `reg 34(1) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 34(1)(a) gather sufficient information about the respondent to understand fully`
    `reg 34(1)(b) determine from publicly-available information from credible sources`
    `reg 34(1)(c) assess the respondent's controls to counter money laundering`
    `reg 34(1)(d) obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new`
    `reg 34(1)(e) document the responsibilities of the respondent and correspondent`
    `reg 34(1)(f) be satisfied that, in respect of those of the respondent's customers`
    `reg 34(1) another measure`

@ref reg 34(1) (src:1086-1094)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 34(1) measure`
`reg 34(1) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 34(1)(a) gather sufficient information about the respondent to understand fully`
    , `reg 34(1)(b) determine from publicly-available information from credible sources`
    , `reg 34(1)(c) assess the respondent's controls to counter money laundering`
    , `reg 34(1)(d) obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new`
    , `reg 34(1)(e) document the responsibilities of the respondent and correspondent`
    , `reg 34(1)(f) be satisfied that, in respect of those of the respondent's customers`

-- reg 34(1): the six measures a correspondent must take, in addition to those in regulation 33.
@ref reg 34(1) (src:1086-1094)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 34(1) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(1) the measure must be taken` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(a) gather sufficient information about the respondent to understand fully` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(b) determine from publicly-available information from credible sources` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(c) assess the respondent's controls to counter money laundering` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(d) obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(e) document the responsibilities of the respondent and correspondent` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(f) be satisfied that, in respect of those of the respondent's customers` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33"
    WHEN `reg 34(1) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the measures and does not close the list

@ref reg 34(1) (src:1086-1094)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 34(1) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 34(1) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(a) gather sufficient information about the respondent to understand fully` THEN JUST "gather sufficient information about the respondent to understand fully the nature of its business"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(b) determine from publicly-available information from credible sources` THEN JUST "determine from publicly-available information from credible sources the reputation of the respondent and the quality of the supervision to which the respondent is subject"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(c) assess the respondent's controls to counter money laundering` THEN JUST "assess the respondent's controls to counter money laundering and terrorist financing"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(d) obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new` THEN JUST "obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new correspondent relationship"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(e) document the responsibilities of the respondent and correspondent` THEN JUST "document the responsibilities of the respondent and correspondent in the correspondent relationship"
    WHEN `reg 34(1)(f) be satisfied that, in respect of those of the respondent's customers` THEN JUST "be satisfied that, in respect of those of the respondent's customers who have direct access to accounts with the correspondent, the respondent— (i) has verified the identity of, and conducts ongoing customer due diligence measures in relation to, such customers; and (ii) is able to provide to the correspondent, upon request, the documents or information obtained when applying such customer due diligence measures"
    WHEN `reg 34(1) another measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

@ref reg 34(1) (src:1086-1094)
GIVEN `the measures taken` IS A LIST OF `reg 34(1) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(1) the measures taken include every measure that the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN measure YIELD elem measure `the measures taken`) `reg 34(1) the entries listed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33" (a measure of (a) to (f) is missing; marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 34(1): who the duty falls on.
-- src:1086 | (1) A credit institution or financial institution (the “correspondent”) which has or proposes to have a correspondent relationship involving the execution of payments with another such institution (the “respondent”) from a third country must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33—
@ref reg 34(1) (src:1086-1086)
GIVEN `the kind of institution` IS A `Kind of relevant person`
      `the institution has or proposes to have a correspondent relationship involving the execution of payments with another credit institution or financial institution (the respondent)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is from a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(1) the correspondent must take the measures that the paragraph lists` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the kind of institution` EQUALS `credit institution` OR `the kind of institution` EQUALS `financial institution`))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A credit institution or financial institution"
        IF `the institution has or proposes to have a correspondent relationship involving the execution of payments with another credit institution or financial institution (the respondent)` AND `the respondent is from a third country`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which has or proposes to have a correspondent relationship involving the execution of payments with another such institution ... from a third country"

-- reg 34(1)(d): "obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new correspondent relationship".
-- A MAYBE DATE: NOTHING means no approval was obtained.  The new relationship has been established on the second date, so a missing approval is a "no".
-- src:1090 | (d) obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new correspondent relationship;
@ref reg 34(1)(d) (src:1090-1090)
GIVEN `the date on which approval from senior management was obtained` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the new correspondent relationship was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(1)(d) approval was obtained before the new correspondent relationship was established` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which approval from senior management was obtained`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "obtain approval from senior management before establishing a new correspondent relationship" (the relationship was established and no approval was obtained)
    WHEN JUST approved THEN
        IF approved LESS THAN `the date on which the new correspondent relationship was established`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before establishing a new correspondent relationship" (approval on or after the day of establishing)

-- reg 34(2): a flat negative.  The answer to "may it?" is the text's no (ruling N2); the prohibition is
-- derived below as a SHANT rule whose bearer the text names.
-- src:1095 | (2) Credit institutions and financial institutions must not enter into, or continue, a correspondent relationship with a shell bank.
@ref reg 34(2) (src:1095-1095)
GIVEN `the kind of institution` IS A `Kind of relevant person`
      `the other party is a shell bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(2) the institution may enter into or continue a correspondent relationship with the other party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the kind of institution` EQUALS `credit institution` OR `the kind of institution` EQUALS `financial institution`))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Credit institutions and financial institutions must not"
        IF `the other party is a shell bank`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not enter into, or continue, a correspondent relationship with a shell bank"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of a relationship "with a shell bank"; paragraph (2) says nothing of any other party

DECLARE `reg 34(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution`

DECLARE `reg 34(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 34(2) enter into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank`
    `reg 34(2) continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank`

@ref reg 34(2) (src:1095-1095)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 34(2) party` `reg 34(2) act`
`reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution must not enter into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution`
    SHANT `reg 34(2) enter into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a credit institution or financial institution entered into a correspondent relationship with a shell bank"

@ref reg 34(2) (src:1095-1095)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 34(2) party` `reg 34(2) act`
`reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution must not continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 34(2) a credit institution or financial institution`
    SHANT `reg 34(2) continue a correspondent relationship with a shell bank`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a credit institution or financial institution continued a correspondent relationship with a shell bank"

-- reg 34(3): the duty falls on a credit institution or financial institution that deals with an institution known to allow shell bank accounts.
-- src:1096 | (3) Credit institutions and financial institutions must take appropriate enhanced measures to ensure that they do not enter into, or continue, a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or financial institution which is known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank.
@ref reg 34(3) (src:1096-1096)
GIVEN `the kind of institution` IS A `Kind of relevant person`
      `the other institution is a credit institution or a financial institution which is known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(3) the institution must take appropriate enhanced measures to ensure it does not enter into or continue the relationship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the kind of institution` EQUALS `credit institution` OR `the kind of institution` EQUALS `financial institution`))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Credit institutions and financial institutions must"
        IF `the other institution is a credit institution or a financial institution which is known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty concerns "a credit institution or financial institution which is known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank"

-- reg 34(4)(a): "correspondent relationship" means ... and including.
-- src:1097 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation—
@ref reg 34(4) (src:1097-1097)
-- src:1098 | (a) “correspondent relationship” means—
-- src:1099 | (i) the provision of banking services by a correspondent to a respondent including providing a current or other liability account and related services, such as cash management, international funds transfers, cheque clearing, providing customers of the respondent with direct access to accounts with the correspondent (and vice versa) and providing foreign exchange services; or
-- src:1100 | (ii) the relationship between and among credit institutions and financial institutions including where similar services are provided by a correspondent to a respondent, and including relationships established for securities transactions or funds transfers;
@ref reg 34(4)(a) (src:1098-1100)
DECLARE `reg 34(4)(a) included service or relationship` IS ONE OF
    `reg 34(4)(a)(i) providing a current or other liability account and related services`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(i) cash management`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(i) international funds transfers`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(i) cheque clearing`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(i) providing customers of the respondent with direct access to accounts with the correspondent (and vice versa)`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(i) providing foreign exchange services`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(ii) a relationship established for securities transactions`
    `reg 34(4)(a)(ii) a relationship established for funds transfers`
    `reg 34(4)(a) another service or relationship`

@ref reg 34(4)(a) (src:1098-1100)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 34(4)(a) included service or relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(4)(a) the service or relationship is included in a correspondent relationship` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(i) providing a current or other liability account and related services` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "including providing a current or other liability account and related services"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(i) cash management` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "such as cash management"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(i) international funds transfers` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "international funds transfers"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(i) cheque clearing` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "cheque clearing"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(i) providing customers of the respondent with direct access to accounts with the correspondent (and vice versa)` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "providing customers of the respondent with direct access to accounts with the correspondent (and vice versa)"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(i) providing foreign exchange services` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "providing foreign exchange services"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(ii) a relationship established for securities transactions` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "including relationships established for securities transactions or funds transfers"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a)(ii) a relationship established for funds transfers` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "including relationships established for securities transactions or funds transfers"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(a) another service or relationship` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including" and "such as" leave other services and relationships open

@ref reg 34(4)(a) (src:1098-1100)
GIVEN `banking services are provided by a correspondent to a respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship is between or among credit institutions and financial institutions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(4)(a) there is a correspondent relationship` MEANS
    IF `banking services are provided by a correspondent to a respondent` OR `the relationship is between or among credit institutions and financial institutions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'correspondent relationship' means"

-- src:1101 | (b) a “shell bank” means a credit institution or financial institution, or an institution engaged in equivalent activities to those carried out by credit institutions or financial institutions, incorporated in a jurisdiction in which it has no physical presence involving meaningful decision-making and management, and which is not part of a financial conglomerate or third-country financial conglomerate;
@ref reg 34(4)(b) (src:1101-1101)
GIVEN `the institution is a credit institution or a financial institution, or an institution engaged in equivalent activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is incorporated in a jurisdiction in which it has no physical presence involving meaningful decision-making and management` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is part of a financial conglomerate or a third-country financial conglomerate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 34(4)(b) the institution is a shell bank` MEANS
    IF `the institution is a credit institution or a financial institution, or an institution engaged in equivalent activities`
       AND `it is incorporated in a jurisdiction in which it has no physical presence involving meaningful decision-making and management`
       AND (NOT `it is part of a financial conglomerate or a third-country financial conglomerate`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'shell bank' means"

-- reg 34(4)(c): two terms are borrowed; the paragraph names where each is defined.
DECLARE `reg 34(4)(c) term` IS ONE OF
    `reg 34(4)(c) financial conglomerate`
    `reg 34(4)(c) third-country financial conglomerate`

-- src:1102 | (c) in sub-paragraph (b), “financial conglomerate” and “third-country financial conglomerate” have the meanings given by regulations 1(2) and 7(1) respectively of the Financial Conglomerates and Other Financial Groups Regulations 2004 .
@ref reg 34(4)(c) (src:1102-1102)
GIVEN term IS A `reg 34(4)(c) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 34(4)(c) the meaning of the term is given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(c) financial conglomerate` THEN "regulation 1(2) of the Financial Conglomerates and Other Financial Groups Regulations 2004"
    WHEN `reg 34(4)(c) third-country financial conglomerate` THEN "regulation 7(1) of the Financial Conglomerates and Other Financial Groups Regulations 2004"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 35 -- politically exposed persons.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Regulation 35 -- Enhanced customer due diligence: politically exposed persons`

-- reg 35(1): every relevant person must have the systems; nothing else conditions the duty.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1104 | (1) A relevant person must have in place appropriate risk-management systems and procedures to determine whether a customer or the beneficial owner of a customer is—
-- src:1105 | (a) a politically exposed person (a “PEP”); or
-- src:1106 | (b) a family member or a known close associate of a PEP,
-- src:1107 | and to manage the enhanced risks arising from the relevant person's business relationship or transactions with such a customer.
@ref reg 35(1) (src:1104-1107)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(1) the relevant person must have in place appropriate risk-management systems and procedures` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` (JUST TRUE)

-- src:1108 | (2) In determining what risk-management systems and procedures are appropriate under paragraph (1), the relevant person must take account of—
-- src:1109 | (a) the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1);
-- src:1110 | (b) the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing inherent in its business;
-- src:1111 | (c) the extent to which that risk would be increased by its business relationship or transactions with a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP, and
-- src:1112 | (d) any relevant information made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47.
@ref reg 35(2) (src:1108-1112)
DECLARE `reg 35(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `reg 35(2)(a) the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)`
    `reg 35(2)(b) the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing inherent`
    `reg 35(2)(c) the extent to which that risk would be increased by its business`
    `reg 35(2)(d) any relevant information made available to the relevant person under`
    `reg 35(2) another matter`

@ref reg 35(2) (src:1108-1112)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 35(2) matter`
`reg 35(2) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 35(2)(a) the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)`
    , `reg 35(2)(b) the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing inherent`
    , `reg 35(2)(c) the extent to which that risk would be increased by its business`
    , `reg 35(2)(d) any relevant information made available to the relevant person under`

-- reg 35(2): the matters to be taken into account in deciding which risk-management systems and procedures are appropriate.
@ref reg 35(2) (src:1108-1112)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 35(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(2) the relevant person must take the matter into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(a) the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of"
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(b) the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing inherent` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of"
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(c) the extent to which that risk would be increased by its business` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of"
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(d) any relevant information made available to the relevant person under` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of"
    WHEN `reg 35(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists the matters and does not close the list

@ref reg 35(2) (src:1108-1112)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 35(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 35(2) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(a) the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)` THEN JUST "the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)"
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(b) the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing inherent` THEN JUST "the level of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing inherent in its business"
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(c) the extent to which that risk would be increased by its business` THEN JUST "the extent to which that risk would be increased by its business relationship or transactions with a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP"
    WHEN `reg 35(2)(d) any relevant information made available to the relevant person under` THEN JUST "any relevant information made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47"
    WHEN `reg 35(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1113 | (3) If a relevant person has determined that a customer or a potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP, the relevant person must assess—
-- src:1114 | (a) the level of risk associated with that customer, and
-- src:1115 | (b) the extent of the enhanced customer due diligence measures to be applied in relation to that customer.
@ref reg 35(3) (src:1113-1115)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has determined that the customer or potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(3) the relevant person must assess the level of risk and the extent of the enhanced customer due diligence measures` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person has determined that the customer or potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a relevant person has determined that a customer or a potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP, the relevant person must assess" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:1116 | (3A) For the purpose of the relevant person’s assessment under paragraph (3), where a customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP—
-- src:1117 | (a) the starting point for the assessment is that the customer or potential customer presents a lower level of risk than a non-domestic PEP, and
@ref reg 35(3A)(a) (src:1116-1117)
GIVEN `the customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(3A)(a) the starting point of the assessment is that the customer presents a lower level of risk than a non-domestic PEP` MEANS
    IF `the customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:1116 | (3A) For the purpose of the relevant person’s assessment under paragraph (3), where a customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP—
-- src:1117 | (a) the starting point for the assessment is that the customer or potential customer presents a lower level of risk than a non-domestic PEP, and
-- src:1118 | (b) if no enhanced risk factors are present, the extent of enhanced customer due diligence measures to be applied in relation to that customer or potential customer is less than the extent to be applied in the case of a non-domestic PEP.
@ref reg 35(3A)(b) (src:1116-1118)
GIVEN `the customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no enhanced risk factors are present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(3A)(b) the extent of the enhanced customer due diligence measures is less than the extent for a non-domestic PEP` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a customer or potential customer is a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `no enhanced risk factors are present`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no enhanced risk factors are present" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- reg 35(4)(a)
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1119 | (4) In assessing the extent of the enhanced customer due diligence measures to be taken in relation to any particular person (which may differ from case to case), a relevant person—
-- src:1120 | (a) must take account of any relevant information made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47; and
@ref reg 35(4)(a) (src:1119-1120)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `relevant information has been made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(4)(a) the relevant person must take account of the relevant information made available to it` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `relevant information has been made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any relevant information made available to the relevant person under regulations 17(9) and 47"; with none made available the paragraph says nothing

-- reg 35(4)(b): a permission ("may"), limited to guidance of two kinds.
-- src:1121 | (b) may take into account any guidance which has been—
-- src:1122 | (i) issued by the FCA; or
-- src:1123 | (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
@ref reg 35(4)(b) (src:1121-1123)
GIVEN `the guidance was issued by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(4)(b) the relevant person may take into account the guidance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance was issued by the FCA` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the guidance was issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` AND `the guidance was approved by the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "guidance which has been issued by the FCA; or issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury"; the paragraph says nothing of other guidance

-- reg 35(5): three requirements on a relevant person who proposes to have, or to continue, a business relationship with a PEP, family member or known close associate.
DECLARE `reg 35(5) requirement` IS ONE OF
    `reg 35(5)(a) have approval from senior management for establishing or continuing the business relationship`
    `reg 35(5)(b) take adequate measures to establish the source of wealth and source of funds`
    `reg 35(5)(c) conduct enhanced ongoing monitoring of the business relationship`

-- SEAM S-8 (asking), SEAM S-K1 (asking, for limb (c))
-- src:1124 | (5) A relevant person who proposes to have, or to continue, a business relationship with a PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a PEP, must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33—
-- src:1125 | (a) have approval from senior management for establishing or continuing the business relationship with that person;
-- src:1126 | (b) take adequate measures to establish the source of wealth and source of funds which are involved in the proposed business relationship or transactions with that person; and
-- src:1127 | (c) where the business relationship is entered into, conduct enhanced ongoing monitoring of the business relationship with that person.
@ref reg 35(5) (src:1124-1127)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person proposes to have, or to continue, a business relationship with a PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
      requirement IS A `reg 35(5) requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(5) the relevant person must meet the requirement, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the answer for a relevant person`
    WHERE
        `the answer for a relevant person` MEANS
            IF (NOT `the relevant person proposes to have, or to continue, a business relationship with a PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a PEP`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant person who proposes to have, or to continue, a business relationship with a PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a PEP"
            ELSE CONSIDER requirement
                 WHEN `reg 35(5)(a) have approval from senior management for establishing or continuing the business relationship` THEN JUST TRUE
                 WHEN `reg 35(5)(b) take adequate measures to establish the source of wealth and source of funds` THEN JUST TRUE
                 WHEN `reg 35(5)(c) conduct enhanced ongoing monitoring of the business relationship` THEN
                     `mlr2 if the condition holds` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` (JUST TRUE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the business relationship is entered into" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- reg 35(6) and (7): long-term insurance.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1128 | (6) A relevant person which is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance (an “insurance policy”) must take reasonable measures to determine whether one or more of the beneficiaries of the insurance policy or the beneficial owner of a beneficiary of such an insurance policy are—
-- src:1129 | (a) PEPs, or
-- src:1130 | (b) family members or known close associates of PEPs.
@ref reg 35(6) (src:1128-1130)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(6) the relevant person must take reasonable measures to determine whether the beneficiaries or their beneficial owners are PEPs or their family members or known close associates` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant person which is providing a customer with a contract of long-term insurance"

-- reg 35(7): "must be taken before (a) any payment is made under the insurance policy, or (b) the benefit of the insurance policy is assigned".
-- src:1131 | (7) The measures required under paragraph (6) must be taken before—
-- src:1132 | (a) any payment is made under the insurance policy, or
-- src:1133 | (b) the benefit of the insurance policy is assigned in whole or in part to another person.
@ref reg 35(7) (src:1131-1133)
GIVEN `the date on which the measures were taken` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which a payment was made under the insurance policy` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the benefit of the insurance policy was assigned` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(7) the measures required by paragraph (6) were taken before any payment was made or the benefit was assigned` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date on which a payment was made under the insurance policy` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the date on which the benefit of the insurance policy was assigned` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither a payment nor an assignment has happened, so the time limit has neither been met nor missed
        IF `the date on which the measures were taken` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be taken before" (a payment or an assignment has happened and the measures have not been taken)
        OTHERWISE `mlr2 both are true` (`before the date` `the date on which the measures were taken` `the date on which a payment was made under the insurance policy`) (`before the date` `the date on which the measures were taken` `the date on which the benefit of the insurance policy was assigned`)
    WHERE
        -- an event that has not happened does not count against the measures
        `before the date` measures event MEANS
            CONSIDER event
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST day THEN
                CONSIDER measures
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be taken before" (the measures have not been taken)
                WHEN JUST taken THEN
                    IF taken LESS THAN day
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be taken before" (taken on or after the day of the payment or the assignment)

-- reg 35(8)
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1134 | (8) A relevant person must, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33, ensure that—
-- src:1135 | (a) its senior management is informed before it pays out any sums under an insurance policy the beneficiary of which is a PEP or a person who comes within paragraph (6)(b) in relation to a PEP, and
@ref reg 35(8)(a) (src:1134-1135)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary of the insurance policy is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP who comes within paragraph (6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(8)(a) the relevant person must ensure that its senior management is informed before it pays out any sums under the insurance policy` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the beneficiary of the insurance policy is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP who comes within paragraph (6)(b)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an insurance policy the beneficiary of which is a PEP or a person who comes within paragraph (6)(b) in relation to a PEP"

-- src:1135 | (a) its senior management is informed before it pays out any sums under an insurance policy the beneficiary of which is a PEP or a person who comes within paragraph (6)(b) in relation to a PEP, and
@ref reg 35(8)(a) (src:1135-1135)
GIVEN `the date on which senior management was informed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the relevant person paid out sums under the insurance policy` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(8)(a) senior management was informed before the sums were paid out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the relevant person paid out sums under the insurance policy`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): nothing has been paid out, so the time limit "before it pays out" has neither been met nor missed
    WHEN JUST paid THEN
        CONSIDER `the date on which senior management was informed`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is informed before it pays out" (sums have been paid out and senior management has not been informed)
        WHEN JUST informed THEN
            IF informed LESS THAN paid
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is informed before it pays out" (informed on or after the day of the pay-out)

-- reg 35(8)(b): the scrutiny applies "whether or not the policy holder is a PEP"; on the reading taken (fork F35-1) it applies to the policy of (a).
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1136 | (b) its entire business relationship with the holder of the insurance policy (“the policy holder”) is scrutinised on an ongoing basis in accordance with enhanced procedures, whether or not the policy holder is a PEP or a family member or known close associate of a PEP.
@ref reg 35(8)(b) (src:1136-1136)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary of the insurance policy is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP who comes within paragraph (6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policy holder is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(8)(b) the relevant person must ensure that its entire business relationship with the policy holder is scrutinised on an ongoing basis in accordance with enhanced procedures` MEANS
    -- `the policy holder is a PEP ...` is not read: "whether or not the policy holder is a PEP or a family member or known close associate of a PEP"
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the beneficiary of the insurance policy is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP who comes within paragraph (6)(b)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the holder of the insurance policy" is the holder of the policy of sub-paragraph (a), whose beneficiary is a PEP or a person within paragraph (6)(b)

-- reg 35(9) to (11): the period after a PEP leaves office.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1137 | (9) Where a person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function, a relevant person must continue to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) in relation to that person—
-- src:1138 | (a) for a period of at least 12 months after the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function; or
-- src:1139 | (b) for such longer period as the relevant person considers appropriate to address risks of money laundering or terrorist financing in relation to that person.
@ref reg 35(9) (src:1137-1139)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person was a PEP and is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function` IS A DATE
      `the longer period that the relevant person considers appropriate ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(9) the relevant person must continue to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) on the date asked` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the answer for a relevant person`
    WHERE
        `twelve months after the date of ceasing` MEANS `add months` `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function` 12
        `the answer for a relevant person` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (NOT `the person was a PEP and is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function`)
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
                IF `the date asked` AT MOST `twelve months after the date of ceasing`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                IF `the date asked is within the longer period`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of at least 12 months after the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function; or for such longer period as the relevant person considers appropriate" (the date asked is after both periods; ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
        `the date asked is within the longer period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the longer period that the relevant person considers appropriate ends on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST end THEN `the date asked` AT MOST end

-- reg 35(10): paragraph (9) does not apply to a person who was not a PEP under the 2007 Regulations and left office before these Regulations came into force.
-- The Money Laundering Regulations 2007 are not among the sources: whether the person was a PEP within regulation 14(5) of them is asked as a fact.
-- src:1140 | (10) Paragraph (9) does not apply in relation to a person who—
-- src:1141 | (a) was not a politically exposed person within the meaning of regulation 14(5) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 , when those Regulations were in force; and
-- src:1142 | (b) ceased to be entrusted with a prominent public function before the date on which these Regulations come into force.
@ref reg 35(10) (src:1140-1142)
GIVEN `the person was a politically exposed person within the meaning of regulation 14(5) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007, when those Regulations were in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the person ceased to be entrusted with a prominent public function` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(10) paragraph (9) does not apply in relation to the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person was a politically exposed person within the meaning of regulation 14(5) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007, when those Regulations were in force`)
       AND `the date on which the person ceased to be entrusted with a prominent public function` LESS THAN `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the disapplication is "in relation to a person who (a) was not a politically exposed person ... and (b) ceased to be entrusted ... before the date on which these Regulations come into force"; for any other person paragraph (10) says nothing

-- The last day of "a period of at least 12 months after the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted" as a value (fork F35-2: the anniversary is included).
-- src:1137 | (9) Where a person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function, a relevant person must continue to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) in relation to that person—
-- src:1138 | (a) for a period of at least 12 months after the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function; or
-- src:1139 | (b) for such longer period as the relevant person considers appropriate to address risks of money laundering or terrorist financing in relation to that person.
@ref reg 35(9) (src:1137-1139)
GIVEN `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 35(9)(a) the last day of the period of at least 12 months` MEANS `add months` `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function` 12

-- reg 35(9) read together with reg 35(10): a person within paragraph (10) is outside paragraph (9).
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
@ref reg 35(9) (src:1137-1139)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person was a PEP and is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function` IS A DATE
      `the longer period that the relevant person considers appropriate ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the person was a politically exposed person within the meaning of regulation 14(5) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007, when those Regulations were in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(9) read with reg 35(10) the relevant person must continue to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) on the date asked` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the answer for a relevant person`
    WHERE
        `the answer for a relevant person` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `reg 35(10) paragraph (9) does not apply in relation to the person`
                       `the person was a politically exposed person within the meaning of regulation 14(5) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007, when those Regulations were in force`
                       `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function`
                   EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (9) does not apply in relation to a person who (a) was not a politically exposed person ... and (b) ceased to be entrusted ... before the date on which these Regulations come into force" (a flat negative, ruling N2)
                OTHERWISE
                    `reg 35(9) the relevant person must continue to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) on the date asked`
                        (JUST TRUE)
                        `the person was a PEP and is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function`
                        `the date on which that person ceased to be entrusted with that public function`
                        `the longer period that the relevant person considers appropriate ends on`
                        `the date asked`

-- reg 35(11)
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1143 | (11) When a person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function, the relevant person is no longer required to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) in relation to a family member or known close associate of that PEP (whether or not the period referred to in paragraph (9) has expired).
@ref reg 35(11) (src:1143-1143)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer is a family member or known close associate of that PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(11) the relevant person is no longer required to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) in relation to the family member or known close associate` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the answer for a relevant person`
    WHERE
        `the answer for a relevant person` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (NOT `the person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function`)
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a person who was a PEP is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
                IF `the customer is a family member or known close associate of that PEP`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the relief is "in relation to a family member or known close associate of that PEP"; for any other customer the paragraph says nothing (a scope limit with no "only", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- reg 35(12)(a) to (f): the definitions.
-- src:1144 | (12) In this regulation—
@ref reg 35(12) (src:1144-1144)
-- src:1145 | (a) “politically exposed person” or “PEP” means an individual who is entrusted with prominent public functions, other than as a middle-ranking or more junior official;
@ref reg 35(12)(a) (src:1145-1145)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entrusted with prominent public functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a middle-ranking or more junior official` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(12)(a) the person is a politically exposed person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND `the person is entrusted with prominent public functions` AND (NOT `the person is a middle-ranking or more junior official`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'politically exposed person' or 'PEP' means an individual who is entrusted with prominent public functions, other than as a middle-ranking or more junior official"

-- src:1146 | (b) “family member” of a politically exposed person includes—
-- src:1147 | (i) a spouse or civil partner of the PEP;
-- src:1148 | (ii) children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's children;
-- src:1149 | (iii) parents of the PEP;
@ref reg 35(12)(b) (src:1146-1149)
DECLARE `reg 35(12)(b) relative` IS ONE OF
    `reg 35(12)(b)(i) a spouse or civil partner of the PEP`
    `reg 35(12)(b)(ii) children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's`
    `reg 35(12)(b)(iii) parents of the PEP`
    `reg 35(12)(b) another relative`

@ref reg 35(12)(b) (src:1146-1149)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 35(12)(b) relative`
`reg 35(12)(b) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 35(12)(b)(i) a spouse or civil partner of the PEP`
    , `reg 35(12)(b)(ii) children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's`
    , `reg 35(12)(b)(iii) parents of the PEP`

-- reg 35(12)(b): relatives who are family members of a politically exposed person (the list is not closed).
@ref reg 35(12)(b) (src:1146-1149)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 35(12)(b) relative`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(12)(b) the relative is a family member of the politically exposed person` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b)(i) a spouse or civil partner of the PEP` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "family member of a politically exposed person includes"
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b)(ii) children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "family member of a politically exposed person includes"
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b)(iii) parents of the PEP` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "family member of a politically exposed person includes"
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b) another relative` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes" leaves other relatives open

@ref reg 35(12)(b) (src:1146-1149)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 35(12)(b) relative`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 35(12)(b) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b)(i) a spouse or civil partner of the PEP` THEN JUST "a spouse or civil partner of the PEP"
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b)(ii) children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's` THEN JUST "children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's children"
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b)(iii) parents of the PEP` THEN JUST "parents of the PEP"
    WHEN `reg 35(12)(b) another relative` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- src:1150 | (c) “known close associate” of a PEP means—
-- src:1151 | (i) an individual known to have joint beneficial ownership of a legal entity or a legal arrangement or any other close business relations with a PEP;
-- src:1152 | (ii) an individual who has sole beneficial ownership of a legal entity or a legal arrangement which is known to have been set up for the benefit of a PEP;
@ref reg 35(12)(c) (src:1150-1152)
GIVEN `the person is an individual known to have joint beneficial ownership of a legal entity or a legal arrangement, or any other close business relations, with a PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual who has sole beneficial ownership of a legal entity or a legal arrangement which is known to have been set up for the benefit of a PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(12)(c) the person is a known close associate of a PEP` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual known to have joint beneficial ownership of a legal entity or a legal arrangement, or any other close business relations, with a PEP`
       OR `the person is an individual who has sole beneficial ownership of a legal entity or a legal arrangement which is known to have been set up for the benefit of a PEP`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'known close associate' of a PEP means"

-- src:1153 | (d) “domestic PEP” means a politically exposed person entrusted with prominent public functions by the United Kingdom;
@ref reg 35(12)(d) (src:1153-1153)
GIVEN `the person is a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entrusted with prominent public functions by the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(12)(d) the person is a domestic PEP` MEANS
    IF `the person is a politically exposed person` AND `the person is entrusted with prominent public functions by the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'domestic PEP' means a politically exposed person entrusted with prominent public functions by the United Kingdom"

-- src:1154 | (e) “non-domestic PEP” means a politically exposed person who is not a domestic PEP;
@ref reg 35(12)(e) (src:1154-1154)
GIVEN `the person is a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a domestic PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(12)(e) the person is a non-domestic PEP` MEANS
    IF `the person is a politically exposed person` AND (NOT `the person is a domestic PEP`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'non-domestic PEP' means a politically exposed person who is not a domestic PEP"

-- reg 35(12)(f): "enhanced risk factors" mean the risk factors other than the person's position as a domestic PEP (or relative or associate of one).
-- src:1155 | (f) “enhanced risk factors”, in relation to a customer or potential customer who is a domestic PEP or a family member or a known close associate of that domestic PEP, mean risk factors other than the customer’s or potential customer’s position as a domestic PEP or as a family member or a known close associate of that domestic PEP.
@ref reg 35(12)(f) (src:1155-1155)
GIVEN `the risk factor is the customer's or potential customer's position as a domestic PEP or as a family member or a known close associate of that domestic PEP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(12)(f) the risk factor is an enhanced risk factor` MEANS
    IF `the risk factor is the customer's or potential customer's position as a domestic PEP or as a family member or a known close associate of that domestic PEP`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "mean risk factors other than the customer's or potential customer's position as a domestic PEP"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- reg 35(13)
-- SEAM S-K2 (asking)
-- src:1156 | (13) For the purposes of paragraph (5), a reference to a business relationship with an individual includes a reference to a business relationship with a person of which the individual is a beneficial owner.
@ref reg 35(13) (src:1156-1156)
GIVEN `the business relationship is with the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 5 and 6 the individual is a beneficial owner of the person the business relationship is with` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(13) the business relationship counts as a business relationship with the individual for the purposes of paragraph (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the business relationship is with the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 5 and 6 the individual is a beneficial owner of the person the business relationship is with` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to a business relationship with a person of which the individual is a beneficial owner" leaves other relationships open; and an unanswered regulation 5 or 6 leaves this one open too

-- src:1157 | (14) For the purposes of paragraphs (9), (11) and (12), individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include—
-- src:1158 | (a) heads of state, heads of government, ministers and deputy or assistant ministers;
-- src:1159 | (b) members of parliament or of similar legislative bodies;
-- src:1160 | (c) members of the governing bodies of political parties;
-- src:1161 | (d) members of supreme courts, of constitutional courts or of any judicial body the decisions of which are not subject to further appeal except in exceptional circumstances;
-- src:1162 | (e) members of courts of auditors or of the boards of central banks;
-- src:1163 | (f) ambassadors, charges d'affaires and high-ranking officers in the armed forces;
-- src:1164 | (g) members of the administrative, management or supervisory bodies of State-owned enterprises;
-- src:1165 | (h) directors, deputy directors and members of the board or equivalent function of an international organisation.
@ref reg 35(14) (src:1157-1165)
DECLARE `reg 35(14) office` IS ONE OF
    `reg 35(14)(a) heads of state, heads of government, ministers and deputy or assistant`
    `reg 35(14)(b) members of parliament or of similar legislative bodies`
    `reg 35(14)(c) members of the governing bodies of political parties`
    `reg 35(14)(d) members of supreme courts, of constitutional courts or of any judicial`
    `reg 35(14)(e) members of courts of auditors or of the boards of central banks`
    `reg 35(14)(f) ambassadors, charges d'affaires and high-ranking officers in the armed`
    `reg 35(14)(g) members of the administrative, management or supervisory bodies`
    `reg 35(14)(h) directors, deputy directors and members of the board or equivalent`
    `reg 35(14) another office`

@ref reg 35(14) (src:1157-1165)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 35(14) office`
`reg 35(14) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 35(14)(a) heads of state, heads of government, ministers and deputy or assistant`
    , `reg 35(14)(b) members of parliament or of similar legislative bodies`
    , `reg 35(14)(c) members of the governing bodies of political parties`
    , `reg 35(14)(d) members of supreme courts, of constitutional courts or of any judicial`
    , `reg 35(14)(e) members of courts of auditors or of the boards of central banks`
    , `reg 35(14)(f) ambassadors, charges d'affaires and high-ranking officers in the armed`
    , `reg 35(14)(g) members of the administrative, management or supervisory bodies`
    , `reg 35(14)(h) directors, deputy directors and members of the board or equivalent`

-- reg 35(14): offices whose holders are individuals entrusted with prominent public functions (the list is not closed).
@ref reg 35(14) (src:1157-1165)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 35(14) office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(14) the holder is an individual entrusted with a prominent public function` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(a) heads of state, heads of government, ministers and deputy or assistant` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(b) members of parliament or of similar legislative bodies` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(c) members of the governing bodies of political parties` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(d) members of supreme courts, of constitutional courts or of any judicial` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(e) members of courts of auditors or of the boards of central banks` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(f) ambassadors, charges d'affaires and high-ranking officers in the armed` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(g) members of the administrative, management or supervisory bodies` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(h) directors, deputy directors and members of the board or equivalent` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "individuals entrusted with prominent public functions include"
    WHEN `reg 35(14) another office` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" leaves other offices open

@ref reg 35(14) (src:1157-1165)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 35(14) office`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 35(14) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(a) heads of state, heads of government, ministers and deputy or assistant` THEN JUST "heads of state, heads of government, ministers and deputy or assistant ministers"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(b) members of parliament or of similar legislative bodies` THEN JUST "members of parliament or of similar legislative bodies"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(c) members of the governing bodies of political parties` THEN JUST "members of the governing bodies of political parties"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(d) members of supreme courts, of constitutional courts or of any judicial` THEN JUST "members of supreme courts, of constitutional courts or of any judicial body the decisions of which are not subject to further appeal except in exceptional circumstances"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(e) members of courts of auditors or of the boards of central banks` THEN JUST "members of courts of auditors or of the boards of central banks"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(f) ambassadors, charges d'affaires and high-ranking officers in the armed` THEN JUST "ambassadors, charges d'affaires and high-ranking officers in the armed forces"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(g) members of the administrative, management or supervisory bodies` THEN JUST "members of the administrative, management or supervisory bodies of State-owned enterprises"
    WHEN `reg 35(14)(h) directors, deputy directors and members of the board or equivalent` THEN JUST "directors, deputy directors and members of the board or equivalent function of an international organisation"
    WHEN `reg 35(14) another office` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 35(15)
-- src:1166 | (15) For the purpose of deciding whether a person is a known close associate of a politically exposed person, a relevant person need only have regard to information which is in its possession, or to credible information which is publicly available.
@ref reg 35(15) (src:1166-1166)
GIVEN `the information is in the relevant person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is credible information which is publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 35(15) the relevant person must have regard to the information in deciding whether a person is a known close associate of a PEP` MEANS
    IF `the information is in the relevant person's possession` OR `the information is credible information which is publicly available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need only have regard to information which is in its possession, or to credible information which is publicly available"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 36 -- politically exposed persons: other duties.  The paragraphs disapply a duty of the
-- Treasury and a duty of the FCA; they bind no one else and mean nothing to a relevant person.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Regulation 36 -- Politically exposed persons: other duties`

DECLARE `reg 36 extent to which the duty is otherwise satisfied` IS ONE OF
    `reg 36 the duty is otherwise satisfied in full`
    `reg 36 the duty is otherwise satisfied in part`
    `reg 36 the duty is not otherwise satisfied`

-- src:1168 | (1) The duty under section 30(1) of the Bank of England and Financial Services Act 2016 (duty to ensure that regulations or orders implementing the fourth money laundering directive comply with paragraphs (a) to (d) of that subsection) does not apply if, and to the extent that, the duty is otherwise satisfied as a result of any provision contained in these Regulations, or any guidance issued by the FCA under these Regulations.
@ref reg 36(1) (src:1168-1168)
GIVEN extent IS A `reg 36 extent to which the duty is otherwise satisfied`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 36(1) the duty under section 30(1) of the Bank of England and Financial Services Act 2016 does not apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER extent
    WHEN `reg 36 the duty is otherwise satisfied in full` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, and to the extent that" -- the paragraph disapplies the duty to the extent only, and the rule does not measure the extent
    WHEN `reg 36 the duty is otherwise satisfied in part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `reg 36 the duty is not otherwise satisfied` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply if, and to the extent that, the duty is otherwise satisfied as a result of any provision contained in these Regulations, or any guidance issued by the FCA under these Regulations"

-- src:1169 | (2) The duty under section 333U(1) and (2) of FSMA (duty to issue guidance in connection with politically exposed persons) does not apply if, and to the extent that, the duty is otherwise satisfied as a result of guidance issued by the FCA under these Regulations.
@ref reg 36(2) (src:1169-1169)
GIVEN extent IS A `reg 36 extent to which the duty is otherwise satisfied`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 36(2) the duty under section 333U(1) and (2) of FSMA does not apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER extent
    WHEN `reg 36 the duty is otherwise satisfied in full` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, and to the extent that" -- the paragraph disapplies the duty to the extent only, and the rule does not measure the extent
    WHEN `reg 36 the duty is otherwise satisfied in part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `reg 36 the duty is not otherwise satisfied` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply if, and to the extent that, the duty is otherwise satisfied as a result of guidance issued by the FCA under these Regulations"
